        "content": "<p>wraitii opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15184\">PR #15184</a> from <code>wraitii:fix/egraph-source-locations</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Found an issue with source tracking while working on a custom jitdump project connected to samply.<br>\nThe investigation &amp; fix were entirely found by GPT Astra, so I cannot vouch for its particular accuracy, but the diff is small and seems to check out for the issue.<br>\nLet me know if I should change something here.</p>\n<h2>Description</h2>\n<p>The egraph elaborator clones instructions during rematerialization and expression placement, but <code>dfg.clone_inst</code> does not copy the separate source-location entry. Surviving instructions can therefore lose their locations, leaving gaps in profiling attribution.</p>\n<p>Copy non-default source locations at both clone sites. Skipping default locations avoids populating an otherwise empty source-location map.</p>\n<p>The regression test checks locations on rematerialized constants and their cloned users. Removing either fix independently makes it fail.</p>\n<p>Validation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>All 1,400 Cranelift filetests pass with <code>all-arch</code>.</li>\n<li><code>cargo fmt --all -- --check</code> passes.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>",
